            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Bakin' Me Crazy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this recipe exactly as written with exception of peppers (we don't care for them and I feel they overpower). The only thing that I think the recipe needs (that isn't written) is it needs to sit for AT LEAST a day. I will make again - 2 days before. I will add the cranberries the day before and the sunflower seeds the day we eat it. Flavors go great together!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sunny22"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Love all of the ingredients and made it 2 times now. The first time I didn’t put the cranberries in-the second time I did. The outcome of the first try was ok but the flavors needed to sink in. After reading other reviews, the second time I mixed everything together and let it sit in the fridge for 24 hours. THAT is the key to this salad!! It was absolutely phenomenal and all the veggies were still crunchy. I mixed it around a couple of times too while it sat. I did not use the sunflower seeds either time. Very colorful salad with lots of flavor! Will certainly make again!",
            "datePublished": "2019-09-07T23:30:20.307Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Rachel Prichard"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Lovely recipe - however I used only 1 Tbsp honey, omitted the cayenne and added 1 tsp minced ginger instead. I also omitted the onion - I can't eat raw onion. Excellent.",
            "datePublished": "2021-07-07T15:05:53.320Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lisa den Elzen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Quite nice. I would reduce the amount of red onion to 1/4 cup and perhaps use two spring onions instead. I used 1/4 cup, not 1/3 of vinegar, and olive oil and l suggest reducing the honey slightly. I would actually reduce the vinegar to less than 1/4 cup. Then taste it and add more if you want to.",
            "datePublished": "2021-02-08T10:05:09.560Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
